<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- Haven round 7, launcher icon ONLY (folds the user's
         "Fold into 7" icon redesign into round 7). REPLACES round
         6's full-bleed Haven leaf green #3E6B2F field: the field
         is now cream/off-white #FAF7F0 (the app's light-theme
         background), full-bleed. The squircle shape itself comes
         from the launcher mask (adaptive icon), not from this
         layer: this layer is the cream fill the mask crops.
         RECENTS (round 6's finding, re-applied): the Fold8
         recents pane can blacken the BACKGROUND layer while the
         foreground survives. If this cream field blackens, the
         foreground house still reads — its mark is BRIGHT
         (lime facets, yellow-orange center, yellow sparkle,
         cream doorway), the inverse of round 5's failure mode
         (a dark mark vanishing into a blackened light field).
         The darkest facet (#3E6B2F) is bounded by bright
         neighbors on both sides, so the silhouette survives
         even where that facet alone goes soft on black. See
         ic_launcher_foreground.xml for the full reasoning. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FAF7F0"
        android:pathData="M0,0 H108 V108 H0 Z" />
</vector>
